+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+Two independent reasons, either of which is sufficient:
+
+1. **The contract cannot function at all against the real USDT contract.** Every call to
+   `deposit()` reverts. The vault would be deployed, funded with nothing, and bricked
+   from block one. Proven on a mainnet fork against the actual token at
+   `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7` (Finding 1).
+2. **Even with that fixed, it is not a yield vault.** The share price is computed from a
+   stored deposit tally that never observes the Aave position. 100% of the Aave interest
+   — measured at 4.26% over one year on the real pool — is permanently stranded and
+   unreachable by anyone, forever (Finding 2). The 0.3% withdrawal fee is stranded the
+   same way, contradicting the README (Findings 3 and 4).
+
+The good news, stated up front so the rest is read in proportion: **the vault is never
+insolvent.** Its Aave position is always greater than or equal to what it owes
+shareholders. Nobody can steal user funds through the accounting — the failure mode is
+value that gets locked away where no one can claim it. The one exception is the owner,
+who has unbounded, un-timelocked power to redirect incoming deposits to themselves
+(Finding 5) and to freeze exits (Finding 6).
+
+---
+
+## Why the suite is green
+
+`forge test` passes 39/39 and `forge coverage` reports 100% of lines and functions.
+Both are true and both are reproduced below. Neither tells you anything about the two
+critical findings, because coverage measures *which lines executed*, not *whether the
+values they produced were right*, and the suite executes those lines against mocks that
+do not behave like the contracts this vault will actually talk to.
+
+| What the vault will talk to on Monday | What the suite tests against | Consequence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `TetherToken` — `approve`/`transfer`/`transferFrom` return **nothing** | `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol`, a stock OpenZeppelin `ERC20` returning `bool` | Finding 1 is invisible |
+| Aave V3 Pool — aUSDT balance grows with the liquidity index | `test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol`, which never pays interest | Finding 2 is invisible |
+| Tether can re-enable a transfer fee via `setParams` at any time | no fee-on-transfer coverage | Finding 7 is invisible |
+
+The suite also contains the withdrawal-fee bug as a *passing assertion*.
+`test_WithdrawReturnsUsdt` (test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol:144) deposits 1000 USDT, withdraws
+everything, and asserts the user gets back 997 USDT. The missing 3 USDT is asserted to
+be correct. Nothing in the suite asks where it went. The answer is: nowhere. See
+Finding 3.
+
