+## How to reproduce everything
+
+Nothing under `src/`, `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol` or `test/mocks/` was modified. Four
+new files were added, all under `test/`:
+
+| File | Contents |
+| --- | --- |
+| `test/audit/VaultAudit.t.sol` | Findings 1–7, offline |
+| `test/audit/MainnetFork.t.sol` | Findings 1 and 2 against real mainnet contracts |
+| `test/audit/VaultInvariant.t.sol` | Foundry invariant run that finds Finding 3 on its own |
+| `test/audit/mocks/AuditMocks.sol` | A faithful Tether stand-in and an Aave pool that actually pays interest |
+
+Every test in these files **asserts the behaviour the README and the NatSpec promise**.
+They fail. Each failure is a finding; the assertion message and the `console2` logs carry
+the numbers.
+
+The fork tests need network access and an archive RPC. They default to the public
+`https://eth.drpc.org`, which worked at the time of writing; override with
+`MAINNET_RPC_URL=<your archive rpc>`. Everything else is offline.
+
+Note that plain `forge test` now runs the fork tests too. Use `--match-contract` as shown
+below to run pieces individually.
