+### Fix (described, not applied)
+
+Replace line 94 with `usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount);`. `SafeERC20` is
+already imported and `using SafeERC20 for IERC20` is already declared at line 20, so
+this is a one-word change. `forceApprove` tolerates a missing return value *and* handles
+Tether's refusal to move a non-zero allowance to another non-zero value by zeroing it
+first.
+
+Better still: set the allowance to `type(uint256).max` once in the constructor
+(or lazily, when it runs low) and drop the per-deposit approval entirely — that removes
+a storage write from every deposit.
+
+Separately, **replace `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` with a no-return-value token** for the
+whole suite. A stock OZ `ERC20` standing in for USDT is the root cause of this class of
+bug going unnoticed, and it will hide the next one too.
