+## Finding 3 — HIGH — the withdrawal fee is destroyed, not redistributed
+
+**Where:** `src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:111–119`
+
+```solidity
+uint256 grossAssets = convertToAssets(shares);
+uint256 fee = (grossAssets * WITHDRAW_FEE_BPS) / BPS_DENOMINATOR;
+netAssets = grossAssets - fee;
+...
+totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets;                          // line 117 — subtracts GROSS
+aavePool.withdraw(address(usdt), netAssets, msg.sender);   // line 119 — removes NET
+```
+
+The README says, twice, in bold prose:
+
+> Both fees stay supplied in Aave and accrue to the remaining shareholders — they are
+> not swept to the owner.
+
+The deposit fee genuinely does that — `deposit` adds the gross `amount` to
+`totalAssetsStored` while minting shares against the net, so the fee lifts the share
+price for everyone already in. That half is correct.
+
+The withdrawal fee does not. Line 117 subtracts the **gross** from the accounting while
+line 119 removes only the **net** from Aave. The fee is deducted from the books and left
+in Aave, so it belongs to no share. Share price is unchanged by a withdrawal (both
+numerator and denominator drop proportionally), so remaining holders gain nothing. The
+value simply leaves the system.
+
+### Evidence
+
+Two depositors of 10,000 USDT each; Alice exits in full; Bob is the only shareholder
+left and should receive Alice's entire ~30 USDT exit fee:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Finding03_WithdrawFeeAccruesToRemainingShareholders -vv
+Ran 1 test for test/audit/VaultAudit.t.sol:VaultAuditTest
+[FAIL: alice's ~30 USDT exit fee must accrue to bob: 9994997499 < 10023997498] test_Finding03_WithdrawFeeAccruesToRemainingShareholders() (gas: 2487697)
+Logs:
+  bob underlying before alice's exit: 9994997498
+  bob underlying after  alice's exit: 9994997499
+  bob gained                        : 1
+  aUSDT still in Aave for the vault : 10025012506
+  vault.totalAssetsStored()         : 9994997499
+  untracked (nobody owns this)      : 30015007
+```
+
+Bob gained **1 base unit** — one ten-thousandth of a cent, pure rounding dust — where
+he should have gained 30.015 USDT. That 30,015,007 base units sits in Aave owned by no
+one.
+
+Note the test also asserts, and passes, that the position matched the accounting exactly
+before the withdrawal. The drift is created by `withdraw`, not by `deposit`.
+
+### Evidence — Foundry's own invariant engine finds this unaided
+
+`test/audit/VaultInvariant.t.sol` drives random deposits and withdrawals across three
+actors over the repo's own untouched mocks:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-contract VaultInvariantTest
