+## Finding 4 — HIGH — stranded value is unrecoverable; there is no rescue path
+
+**Where:** whole contract — the absence of a function
+
+Findings 2 and 3 both park USDT in Aave that no share can redeem. There is no owner
+sweep, no `rescueTokens`, no `skim`, and the contract is not upgradeable. Once all
+shares are burned the vault owns aUSDT with `totalShares == 0`, and every path to it is
+closed.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Finding04_NothingIsLeftBehindAfterFullExit -vv
+Ran 1 test for test/audit/VaultAudit.t.sol:VaultAuditTest
+[FAIL: no USDT may be left stranded once all shares are burned: 59999999 != 0] test_Finding04_NothingIsLeftBehindAfterFullExit() (gas: 2493998)
+Logs:
+  totalShares after full exit : 0
+  totalAssetsStored           : 0
+  aUSDT stranded in Aave      : 59999999
+```
+
+Two 10,000 USDT deposits, both fully withdrawn: **59.999999 USDT gone** — the 0.3%
+withdrawal fee from each exit — with zero shares outstanding and zero assets on the
+books. On the mocks, which pay no interest. On mainnet the interest from Finding 2 is
+added on top and grows without bound.
+
+Any new depositor arriving afterwards mints at a share price of 1.0 and inherits none
+of it.
+
+### Fix (described, not applied)
+
+Fixing Findings 2 and 3 removes the cause. Regardless, add a defensive
+owner-only `skim(address to)` that withdraws
+`aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this)) - totalAssets()` — the provably unowned surplus only,
+never principal — so that an accounting bug is recoverable rather than terminal. Guard
+it with the timelock from Finding 5.
